WEBVTT

00:08.222 --> 00:12.722
That's Deadly Queen…
I named him myself.

00:14.228 --> 00:16.605
I will eradicate you,

00:16.647 --> 00:19.358
and will sleep soundly tonight.

00:20.443 --> 00:23.279
I warned you. Don't move!

00:23.362 --> 00:25.113
Harvest takes no prisoners!

00:30.244 --> 00:31.912
Such a profuse welcome.

00:31.996 --> 00:34.123
Though crushing
three or four of them

00:34.206 --> 00:35.498
leaves you completely unscathed.

00:36.584 --> 00:38.127
Move another centimeter,

00:38.169 --> 00:41.255
and I'll slice that… whatever that
big artery is in your neck!

00:41.589 --> 00:44.675
Oh, yeah, your carotid!
I'll slash your carotid artery!

00:44.759 --> 00:48.554
I'll hack it to pieces!
My Harvest is invincible!

00:49.055 --> 00:51.140
By the looks of your Stand,

00:51.182 --> 00:55.682
it's the powerful, short-range type.

00:55.811 --> 00:58.939
I'm guessing it's got one,
maybe two meters.

00:59.231 --> 01:02.442
If dying's your goal,
then go ahead and make your move.

01:03.653 --> 01:05.321
Interesting…

01:05.363 --> 01:09.492
So each user is endowed with
a unique ability?

01:10.451 --> 01:14.121
Stand? Hmm… Stand, eh?

01:14.955 --> 01:16.331
I should tell you,

01:16.415 --> 01:20.915
Deadly Queen also has what
you might call a unique ability…

01:22.505 --> 01:25.216
He has something… Grab it!

01:27.343 --> 01:30.179
Huh? A 100-yen coin?

01:30.221 --> 01:32.097
Whatcha gonna do with this?

01:32.598 --> 01:37.098
I thought I'd reveal just
what makes Deadly Queen so unique.

01:37.895 --> 01:41.523
Being that you might
as well already be dead.

01:42.608 --> 01:45.193
Deadly Queen has the power…

01:45.319 --> 01:49.819
to transform anything
it touches into a bomb.

01:50.658 --> 01:52.201
Anything…

01:53.661 --> 01:56.038
Even a 100-yen coin.

01:57.623 --> 02:00.542
Drop the coin, Harvest!

02:11.679 --> 02:15.849
Now, a gentle night of
glorious sleep awaits.

02:35.578 --> 02:36.328
JOJO'S BIZARRE ADVENTURE
DIAMOND IS UNBREAKABLE

02:36.328 --> 02:38.455
<i>A demon's crept into
our everyday life</i>

02:38.539 --> 02:40.832
<i>It's about to take away
something precious</i>

02:40.875 --> 02:44.128
<i>Our peace has already
crumbled long ago</i>

02:44.879 --> 02:47.006
<i>So casually, so nonchalantly</i>

02:47.047 --> 02:49.424
<i>It's taken from us
before we know it</i>

02:49.467 --> 02:52.720
<i>If we want it back,
now's the chance</i>

02:52.928 --> 02:56.431
<i>With the sharpness of
the piercing arrow</i>

02:57.224 --> 03:00.644
<i>The beauty of two souls united</i>

03:00.728 --> 03:03.313
<i>Wherever you go, chase you</i>

03:03.397 --> 03:05.524
<i>Whenever, chase you</i>

03:05.566 --> 03:07.609
<i>I will chase you</i>

03:07.651 --> 03:09.277
<i>Nowhere to escape</i>

03:09.361 --> 03:11.946
<i>Start running, I will chase you</i>

03:11.989 --> 03:14.032
<i>Tomorrow, chase you</i>

03:14.074 --> 03:16.785
<i>My fists will be the one
to show you</i>

03:16.994 --> 03:21.494
<i>Tenacity decides
who will win or lose</i>

03:22.708 --> 03:27.208
<i>So I chase you</i>

03:30.508 --> 03:34.720
EPISODE 22
YOSHIKAGE KIRA JUST
WANTS TO LIVE QUIETLY, PART 2

03:33.594 --> 03:34.741
Have you heard?

03:34.804 --> 03:36.639
Some beauty clinic says
it'll help you find true love.

03:36.847 --> 03:39.599
Huh? Seriously? That's hilarious.

03:39.642 --> 03:42.144
It's true! I heard some
high schooler found success!

03:43.103 --> 03:45.438
So a single blast
wasn't enough to knock him off…

03:46.649 --> 03:50.653
W-What did he do to me? What…

03:51.070 --> 03:52.071
What the…?

03:57.076 --> 03:59.953
What happened to me?!

03:59.995 --> 04:01.246
I told you.

04:01.288 --> 04:02.956
Deadly Queen has the ability to

04:02.998 --> 04:05.583
transform anything
it touches into a bomb.

04:05.626 --> 04:08.462
You see, that's what
I did with this 100-yen coin.

04:08.921 --> 04:11.340
I press the detonator
at my leisure,

04:11.382 --> 04:15.386
and my victim is blown
to smithereens from the inside out.

04:15.803 --> 04:17.721
Though, it seems in
your case, Shigechi,

04:17.805 --> 04:21.266
the blast has partially
imploded your face,

04:21.308 --> 04:25.808
creating a human cocktail of
facial fascia and cerebral tissue.

04:27.606 --> 04:30.650
Before I deliver one final blast,

04:30.693 --> 04:33.362
there's something I must confirm.

04:33.946 --> 04:36.198
This power you refer to
as a "Stand"…

04:36.323 --> 04:40.368
Josuke and Okuyasu wield
the power of the Stand, too, yes?

04:40.870 --> 04:42.872
H-Help me…

04:42.955 --> 04:46.208
No, no, no, no, no, no, no.

04:46.333 --> 04:48.460
You simply must die.

04:48.669 --> 04:51.463
I can't have a witness
alive and kicking.

04:51.589 --> 04:53.382
Not a single living soul must ever be

04:53.465 --> 04:57.635
able to possess knowledge of
the true Yoshikage Kira.

04:58.220 --> 05:02.349
But you see,
Stand users intrigue me.

05:02.683 --> 05:04.559
I have no doubt
I could find out myself,

05:04.727 --> 05:07.688
but there's no substitute
for the genuine article.

05:08.355 --> 05:10.106
Josuke, Okuyasu…

05:10.649 --> 05:12.400
Who are the others?

05:13.360 --> 05:16.196
How many more are in this town?

05:17.156 --> 05:18.407
What are their powers?

05:18.782 --> 05:21.284
I-I don't know…

05:21.785 --> 05:23.995
Come now, you must know.

05:24.121 --> 05:26.915
Listen, if you refuse
to spill the beans…

05:27.541 --> 05:29.793
I will kill your parents, too.

05:30.794 --> 05:31.753
Wha…

05:32.546 --> 05:34.756
What?

05:34.924 --> 05:37.801
Mommy and Daddy?

05:37.927 --> 05:39.511
Hurry up and spit it out.

05:39.553 --> 05:42.013
Do that,
and I'll leave them alone.

05:42.056 --> 05:45.517
Quit stalling.
I want this between the two of us.

05:45.851 --> 05:48.812
Names are good enough.
Come on, hurry it up.

05:49.396 --> 05:51.606
E-Everyone said so…

05:51.690 --> 05:55.777
There's a murderer in this town,
and they're lookin' for him!

05:55.903 --> 05:59.865
A murderer… They meant you!

05:59.907 --> 06:03.368
You killed Reimi Sugimoto, too!

06:03.410 --> 06:05.453
What? Reimi Sugimoto?!

06:06.705 --> 06:10.166
The shit can still
use his Stand?

06:11.085 --> 06:12.127
Deadly Queen!

06:18.634 --> 06:20.302
That brat…

06:20.636 --> 06:22.471
To think I practically
tore him to pieces…

06:30.729 --> 06:35.229
I-I have to get to Josuke…

06:38.445 --> 06:42.323
Josuke's Shining Diamond…

06:43.617 --> 06:47.912
can fix me…

06:50.916 --> 06:55.416
I have to protect
Mommy and Daddy…

06:57.172 --> 07:01.672
I have to keep Mommy and Daddy
safe from him!

07:03.053 --> 07:06.681
That horrible, rotten man

07:07.182 --> 07:11.682
can't be in the same town
as my mommy and daddy!

07:12.229 --> 07:14.022
HIGH SCHOOL AHEAD
NO MIDDLE SCHOOL STUDENTS
BEYOND THIS POINT
- MIDDLE SCHOOL PRINCIPAL

07:18.652 --> 07:20.695
I have to…

07:22.322 --> 07:25.616
reach Josuke…

07:28.537 --> 07:29.871
Oh, sorry.

07:30.748 --> 07:32.291
Are you okay?

07:33.167 --> 07:35.544
I have to…

07:35.586 --> 07:37.713
What's the matter?

07:37.755 --> 07:39.840
He's a middle schooler.

07:42.509 --> 07:44.219
Something's seriously wrong
with him.

07:44.553 --> 07:46.179
Let's get a teacher…

07:46.180 --> 07:48.599
No, leave him alone.
He's weird.

07:49.224 --> 07:50.516
Let's go.

07:56.023 --> 07:59.234
J-Josuke!

08:04.198 --> 08:06.658
J-Josuke!

08:14.041 --> 08:17.127
Everyone's looking for me, huh?

08:17.211 --> 08:19.213
Do you mean there's someone
in this town

08:19.254 --> 08:22.465
who knows about
Reimi Sugimoto's murder?

08:23.550 --> 08:27.011
You are aware, no one will ever
be able to track me down…

08:27.971 --> 08:31.599
No one knows
Yoshikage Kira's true colors.

08:32.226 --> 08:35.771
As long as you are no more…

08:37.147 --> 08:40.775
<i>I'm gonna protect
Mommy and Daddy…</i>

08:42.402 --> 08:46.197
Deadly Queen has already
left its mark on the doorknob.

08:51.745 --> 08:54.748
Josuke!

09:00.003 --> 09:03.006
Behold the genius of Deadly Queen.

09:04.424 --> 09:07.468
And with that,
the evidence has been destroyed.

09:07.678 --> 09:10.263
Did someone just call my name?

09:10.556 --> 09:12.140
Yeah, without a doubt.

09:12.224 --> 09:14.893
H-Hey, Josuke, look!

09:21.650 --> 09:25.487
Got… it!

09:26.405 --> 09:28.281
Sh-Shigechi?!

09:30.492 --> 09:31.993
Shigechi!

09:32.870 --> 09:35.289
S-Something's not right, Josuke!

09:35.330 --> 09:37.999
Harvest was hobbling around
spurting blood before disappearing.

09:38.083 --> 09:40.502
That's not how Stands disappear!

09:40.627 --> 09:43.921
Why did just one of 'em
come to see us?

09:49.970 --> 09:51.846
We need to go to
the middle school.

09:52.014 --> 09:53.598
We have to find Shigechi!

09:56.768 --> 10:00.188
Interesting.
Where did I lose that?

10:00.647 --> 10:02.607
Nothing to worry about now.

10:03.066 --> 10:07.070
I do hope my tailor carries
the same button…

10:22.836 --> 10:25.004
No, I don't believe it…

10:26.089 --> 10:29.467
It's happened again.
He's done it again…

10:31.595 --> 10:34.306
Another victim screams
across the skies…

10:35.599 --> 10:38.393
They must have crossed paths.

10:45.234 --> 10:46.360
Shigechi…

11:00.874 --> 11:02.250
There's no question.

11:02.542 --> 11:03.751
This boy has passed.

11:05.170 --> 11:08.882
Shigekiyo and he met,
he killed Shigekiyo.

11:09.508 --> 11:10.926
I have no doubt.

11:11.718 --> 11:15.763
Why they crossed paths,
how he was murdered,

11:15.973 --> 11:17.224
that I cannot tell you.

11:17.891 --> 11:19.642
It was his work.

11:20.477 --> 11:23.855
It's the handiwork of
the man who killed me.

11:25.399 --> 11:28.110
I looked for Shigechi,
but couldn't find him anywhere.

11:28.610 --> 11:30.653
He disappeared in
the five minutes

11:30.737 --> 11:32.947
Okuyasu and I were
separated from him.

11:34.074 --> 11:38.574
Shigechi's books and school supplies
were just as he had left them,

11:39.579 --> 11:42.248
and his parents have filed
a missing person report with the police.

11:43.250 --> 11:44.167
I'd say this is…

11:44.584 --> 11:48.379
Y-You mean…
The culprit is a Stand user?

11:50.257 --> 11:54.094
You guys wouldn't know this,

11:54.136 --> 11:58.098
but Shigechi's Harvest
is practically unbeatable.

11:58.348 --> 12:00.808
This guy managed to kill Shigechi
in five minutes,

12:00.892 --> 12:03.853
and take his body from
the school and hide it somehow.

12:04.438 --> 12:08.938
Jotaro, it's clear we have
a Stand user on our hands,

12:09.484 --> 12:12.028
the rest of us
can't just stand idle.

12:12.779 --> 12:13.654
Josuke.

12:13.947 --> 12:15.448
You found a button, right.

12:15.532 --> 12:19.327
Yeah… Harvest brought it to me.

12:19.828 --> 12:20.829
This is it.

12:22.622 --> 12:24.582
This is Shigechi's dying word.

12:25.125 --> 12:29.625
Harvest may have managed to
pull it off the murderer's clothes.

12:31.089 --> 12:33.007
I'll hold on to this.

12:33.467 --> 12:34.468
I'd like to investigate it further.

12:34.551 --> 12:38.680
Y-You can find the guy
with that run-of-the-mill button?

12:38.930 --> 12:40.139
It's possible.

12:40.515 --> 12:41.849
We might be able to find
the brand and manufacturer

12:41.892 --> 12:44.019
of the clothes it belongs to.

12:44.353 --> 12:45.520
It makes sense…

12:45.979 --> 12:50.316
I-If we're done talking,
I'm gonna go home.

12:51.693 --> 12:54.362
All of this has put me
in a weird mood.

12:54.654 --> 12:56.489
I-I'm really pissed…

12:57.115 --> 12:58.783
Let's go home, Dad.

13:00.452 --> 13:02.829
Okuyasu's just not himself today.

13:02.996 --> 13:07.496
Yeah… Shigechi may've
been an annoying, greedy bastard,

13:08.377 --> 13:10.921
but there was something
undeniably lovable about him.

13:11.838 --> 13:14.173
I can't believe he's gone.

13:15.342 --> 13:16.718
It's the kind of thing

13:16.760 --> 13:20.597
where you don't know whether
you should scream or cry.

13:21.056 --> 13:23.475
It's irritating as all hell.

13:23.600 --> 13:25.143
We all feel that way.

13:25.811 --> 13:28.188
I'm sure Okuyasu feels it worse.

13:29.022 --> 13:30.398
Damn it…

13:30.774 --> 13:34.235
Something horrific was happening,
and I had no idea.

13:34.569 --> 13:38.155
I'll sound the alarm
to all my customers.

13:38.490 --> 13:41.117
Sigh… I can't imagine
he'd pay me a visit,

13:41.201 --> 13:43.161
but for good measure…

13:43.537 --> 13:46.790
Stand users are always
drawn to each other…

13:47.124 --> 13:49.501
Though I hope I never have
the misfortune of meeting him.

13:50.752 --> 13:53.421
So I suppose we must
all step up and act now, huh?

14:19.239 --> 14:19.989
<i>Oh?</i>

14:20.615 --> 14:22.617
<i>That was definitely Josuke…</i>

14:24.870 --> 14:26.454
And Okuyasu, too.

14:27.330 --> 14:29.165
Listen, you won't believe it.

14:30.083 --> 14:32.877
Remember how it was
my birthday last Friday?

14:32.961 --> 14:37.461
Well, that guy I'm seeing
gave me this really shitty ring.

14:38.800 --> 14:41.135
Look at it!
I can't wear this thing.

14:41.428 --> 14:45.306
For now I have to be like,
"Oh, my god I love it!"

14:45.515 --> 14:47.850
I was only going out with him
cause his dad owns some land.

14:47.934 --> 14:49.477
He's a total hick.

14:49.603 --> 14:53.481
It really looks like some toy ring.
How much was it?

14:53.607 --> 14:55.650
I'm guessing like 150,000 yen.

14:55.942 --> 14:58.110
I bet a pawn shop will
give you something for it.

14:58.195 --> 15:01.489
I can't let it ugly up
these beautiful fingers.

15:03.366 --> 15:05.534
<i>Her soul is grotesque,</i>

15:05.702 --> 15:08.496
<i>but her hands and face
are beautiful…</i>

15:08.872 --> 15:10.498
<i>Come my way,</i>

15:10.582 --> 15:13.209
<i>and I'll set that soul right
and show you a glorious time.</i>

15:13.376 --> 15:15.920
Well, gotta go.
See you later.

15:16.087 --> 15:17.505
Okay, bye-bye!

15:22.594 --> 15:24.721
I'm afraid it's good bye for now.

15:24.846 --> 15:26.722
Let's keep this
as painless as possible.

15:31.686 --> 15:34.939
SHIGEKIYO YANGU: DECEASED
STAND: HARVEST

15:38.735 --> 15:41.529
DEADLY QUEEN

15:50.080 --> 15:53.583
<i>Good morning,
and welcome to Morioh Radio.</i>

15:53.667 --> 15:55.210
<i>This is Kai Harada,</i>

15:55.293 --> 15:57.378
<i>your easy listen in'
disc jockey extraordinaire.</i>

15:57.462 --> 16:00.381
<i>Is everyone ready for
a beautiful week?</i>

16:00.799 --> 16:03.134
<i>It's hard to believe,
only three days left in June.</i>

16:03.176 --> 16:05.553
<i>-And once it's July,</i>
- Well, let's dig in.

16:05.637 --> 16:07.180
<i>- You know what that means…</i>
- Oh, that's right.

16:07.222 --> 16:08.556
<i>- That's right. Summer vacation.</i>
- I've got several places

16:08.640 --> 16:10.141
<i>- So what's in store?</i>
- to drop by today,

16:10.183 --> 16:12.977
<i>- I know I can't wait.</i>
- so I'd like you to stay put.

16:13.353 --> 16:17.190
<i>- And now, while the clouds are away,</i>
- We'll dine together tonight when I return.

16:17.232 --> 16:21.069
<i>A fresh jam fitting for this fine day</i>

16:22.946 --> 16:25.698
Thankfully they still
had some of the Parisian specials.

16:25.740 --> 16:28.409
- Talk about lucky!
- Let's get a move on to Yohei Lake.

16:28.493 --> 16:29.911
Wait, Asuka's not here yet.

16:29.953 --> 16:34.453
- What? What's taking her so long?
<i>- It's been four days since that day…</i>

16:37.419 --> 16:40.422
<i>It's been pretty quiet, but…</i>

16:43.133 --> 16:46.928
<i>It doesn't change that a killer
is still lurking somewhere in this town.</i>

16:48.138 --> 16:51.641
<i>When it comes down to it,
the mind sees what it wants to see.</i>

16:52.058 --> 16:55.519
<i>The look of guilt and innocence
is in the eye of the beholder.</i>

17:04.070 --> 17:07.156
Oh… H-Hi, Mr. Jotaro.

17:08.742 --> 17:11.870
Um, did you find anything
out of the ordinary?

17:12.912 --> 17:16.457
Anything about
the murderer's button, or…

17:16.875 --> 17:18.334
No, not quite.

17:19.044 --> 17:20.545
Nothing to speak of yet.

17:21.504 --> 17:23.297
I-I see…

17:28.470 --> 17:31.306
Um, where are you headed?

17:33.099 --> 17:35.476
Nowhere special.

17:36.019 --> 17:37.270
Over there I suppose.

17:37.520 --> 17:38.771
Ah…

17:41.941 --> 17:43.317
<i>Good lord…</i>

17:43.401 --> 17:46.320
<i>Getting the strong, silent type
to chat is like pulling teeth.</i>

17:46.613 --> 17:48.906
<i>Rohan-Sensei's pushiness
is unsettling,</i>

17:48.948 --> 17:51.659
<i>but Jotaro's silence sends me
into a panic.</i>

17:52.035 --> 17:55.663
<i>There's gotta be something
we can talk about… Let's see…</i>

17:56.956 --> 17:59.166
That coat is really terrific,
you know that!

18:01.044 --> 18:05.544
CENTIPEDE SHOES

18:01.836 --> 18:04.088
Looks like we've found
a shoe store.

18:04.172 --> 18:07.633
Huh? Oh! Yes, a shoe store
it certainly is.

18:08.176 --> 18:09.532
Is there something wrong?

18:09.552 --> 18:14.052
WE DO SIMPLE TAILORING

18:11.971 --> 18:14.682
It's a shoe store, but
they also do simple alterations,

18:14.808 --> 18:19.308
like skirt waists and
pant hemming on the side.

18:20.105 --> 18:22.357
There's also an electronics shop
that sells flowers.

18:22.649 --> 18:24.400
Is there something wrong?

18:24.693 --> 18:27.487
I heard all about
the tailors of Morioh,

18:28.029 --> 18:31.095
But I didn't think to ask
about places like this.

18:38.498 --> 18:40.708
Something wrong with this button?

18:40.959 --> 18:44.212
No, if it doesn't ring a bell,
forget it.

18:44.546 --> 18:48.132
I just couldn't remember what
it was originally attached to.

18:49.384 --> 18:52.720
ANIMAL CRACKERS

18:49.843 --> 18:52.742
Hey kid, want an animal cracker?

18:53.221 --> 18:57.721
I save the camels for last,
so everything else is fair game.

18:58.893 --> 19:00.644
Thanks but, I'm fine.

19:00.770 --> 19:02.104
I see.

19:02.731 --> 19:05.608
You know, not only
have I seen that button,

19:05.900 --> 19:07.318
but have a look.

19:07.360 --> 19:10.571
I just finished working on
the suit that button belongs to.

19:10.947 --> 19:12.949
A customer came in yesterday,

19:13.032 --> 19:15.701
asking me to put on
the exact same button.

19:16.953 --> 19:19.246
See? Looks like
the same button to me.

19:19.622 --> 19:20.789
Jotaro!

19:20.874 --> 19:23.710
Good grief.
We found it, Koichi.

19:23.877 --> 19:25.128
Found it?

19:25.336 --> 19:26.545
Oh, n-nothing…

19:26.713 --> 19:29.048
Forget that, what did
this customer look like?

19:29.215 --> 19:30.633
Did you catch a name?

19:31.009 --> 19:32.135
His name?

19:32.218 --> 19:35.429
Well, of course I did.
Do you take me for an idiot?

19:35.680 --> 19:39.308
I remember all of
my customers' names.

19:39.684 --> 19:43.020
Anything less would
be rude to the customer.

19:43.188 --> 19:45.773
Thousands or hundreds of
thousands makes no difference!

19:45.982 --> 19:46.732
Is that so?

19:47.817 --> 19:51.862
Yes! That's amazing!
Could you tell us his name?

19:54.073 --> 19:58.573
Anyway, the jacket
has the order tag.

19:59.454 --> 20:00.997
Of course, I don't need that…

20:01.080 --> 20:03.290
I can remember hundreds
of my customer's names.

20:03.917 --> 20:06.586
It's just faster this way.

20:12.133 --> 20:13.697
Let's see…

20:12.592 --> 20:13.676
KIRA

20:14.302 --> 20:17.305
Now how do you read
this last name?

20:18.223 --> 20:19.432
It must be…

20:19.474 --> 20:22.810
W-What is it?
Please show me.

20:23.269 --> 20:26.313
Um… Um…

20:43.832 --> 20:45.291
Over here.

20:46.835 --> 20:50.004
W-What the?! My hand!

20:50.255 --> 20:52.090
Over here.

20:52.173 --> 20:54.675
J-Jotaro! L-Look!

20:54.759 --> 20:57.636
Watch it, Koichi!
Don't get any closer!

20:57.679 --> 21:01.683
Hey, I said look over here.

21:13.736 --> 21:15.112
Is that his Stand?!

21:18.783 --> 21:20.451
J-Jotaro!

21:21.870 --> 21:25.248
H-He's here!
He's taking the jacket!

21:27.166 --> 21:30.002
To think someone would go
as far as

21:30.044 --> 21:33.797
to investigate the button
that fell off my jacket…

21:33.923 --> 21:37.468
Did they gaze upon
the name Yoshikage Kira?

21:38.011 --> 21:40.972
Why have I been weighed down
with nothing but adversity lately?

21:41.681 --> 21:43.015
Good grief.

21:43.057 --> 21:45.100
Of course he comes
to get his suit now…

21:46.227 --> 21:48.229
But I shall
make them evaporate

21:48.271 --> 21:51.732
with Deadly Queen's second bomb.

21:51.941 --> 21:54.735
Like that pathetic punk, Shigechi…

21:56.487 --> 21:58.113
It's moving again!

21:58.865 --> 22:00.408
Our evidence!

22:00.450 --> 22:01.325
Wait!

22:01.784 --> 22:03.535
We can't just blindly go after it.

22:03.745 --> 22:06.539
Something's not right about
the way he's pulling the jacket.

22:15.882 --> 22:17.341
This Stand…

22:20.887 --> 22:22.513
Careful… It's gonna blow!

23:38.798 --> 23:42.009
EPISODE 23
HEART ATTACK, PART 1
